From c5011d4fcec844f6cfa74ece0a9ba6ea74ce932e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:55:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] slip: optional SLIP-over-UART link to an external HaLow
 (RNode) modem
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lets RNSBox use an external WiFi-HaLow RNode modem as a long-range sub-GHz
Reticulum interface over a 3-wire UART, using SLIP (IP-over-serial). rnsd
reaches the modem as a normal TCPClientInterface. Opt-in, OFF by default.

- kernel: CONFIG_SLIP=y (SLIP is under NETDEVICES, outside NET_CORE, depends
  only on TTY).
- buildroot: BR2_PACKAGE_UTIL_LINUX_BINARIES=y for ldattach (attaches the
  N_SLIP line discipline). busybox stty sets the non-standard 1.5 Mbaud first,
  since musl's ldattach -s cannot.
- S31slip init + /etc/rnsbox/slip.conf: when enabled, set the line speed with
  stty then ldattach SLIP on the UART and bring up a point-to-point sl0
  (local_ip peer peer_ip). No-op when disabled, the device is absent, or the
  modem isn't wired. Does not touch eth0/usb0.
- portal (Reticulum tab): a 'HaLow modem (SLIP)' card — enable/disable, UART
  device, baud, local/peer IP, live sl0 status; store.read/write_slip_conf,
  sysinfo.slip_status, applied live via S31slip reload.
- portal: reverse-proxy the modem's own web UI through the portal, behind
  @login_required, at /modem/ — it serves the modem's self-contained config
  page with its /api/ fetches rewritten to /modem/api/ and proxies those over
  sl0. An 'Open modem web UI' button sits on the card. This reuses the portal
  login to gate the modem instead of exposing it via an unauthenticated LAN
  DNAT. (OTA upload through the proxy can exceed MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH; flash the
  modem over its own Ethernet UI.)
- portal: carrierless interfaces (sl0, tun) report operstate 'unknown' even
  when fully up, which the UI flagged as a scary badge. sysinfo now resolves
  an admin-up 'unknown' interface that has carrier to 'up', so the
  All-interfaces table shows UP rather than a false alarm.
- docs: README.RNSBox.md 'Connecting a WiFi-HaLow modem' section.

Wiring (Nano-e): UART1 GPIOA28 TX / A29 RX (/dev/ttyS1), 3.3 V. The Nano UART
maxes at 1,562,500 baud (25 MHz/16), so the modem must be set to 1.5 Mbaud.
